{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class C {\n    static final int INF = (int)1e6;\n    static int[][][][] mem;\n    static String s;\n\n    static int rec(int i, int p, int n, int c) {\n        int tc = c - 50;\n        if (i == 17) {\n            return (p + n + tc == 0) ? 0 : INF;\n        }\n        if (mem[i][p][n][c] != -1) return mem[i][p][n][c];\n        int best = INF;\n        int mp = Math.min(15, p);\n        int mn = Math.min(15, n);\n        for (int a = 0; a <= mp; a++) {\n            for (int b = 0; b <= mn; b++) {\n                int sum = p - n + tc;\n                int dig = (sum % 10 + 10) % 10;\n                int nc = sum > 0 ? sum / 10 : (sum - 9) / 10;\n                if (dig != s.charAt(i) - '0') continue;\n                int cost = rec(i + 1, p - a, n - b, nc + 50) + (a + b) * (i + 1);\n                if (cost < best) best = cost;\n            }\n        }\n        mem[i][p][n][c] = best;\n        return best;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long val = sc.nextLong();\n        int cap = 50;\n        mem = new int[20][cap][cap][100];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < cap; j++) {\n                for (int k = 0; k < cap; k++) {\n                    Arrays.fill(mem[i][j][k], -1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        s = Long.toString(val);\n        while (s.length() < 17) s = \"0\" + s;\n        s = new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString();\n        int res = INF;\n        for (int pos = 0; pos < cap; pos++) {\n            for (int neg = 0; neg < cap; neg++) {\n                int cand = rec(0, pos, neg, 50);\n                if (cand < res) res = cand;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(res);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstring>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int INF = 1000000;\nint mem[20][50][50][100];\nstring s;\n\nint rec(int i, int p, int n, int c) {\n    int tc = c - 50;\n    if (i == 17) {\n        return (p + n + tc == 0) ? 0 : INF;\n    }\n    if (mem[i][p][n][c] != -1) return mem[i][p][n][c];\n    int best = INF;\n    int mp = min(15, p);\n    int mn = min(15, n);\n    for (int a = 0; a <= mp; a++) {\n        for (int b = 0; b <= mn; b++) {\n            int sum = p - n + tc;\n            int dig = (sum % 10 + 10) % 10;\n            int nc = sum > 0 ? sum / 10 : (sum - 9) / 10;\n            if (dig != s[i] - '0') continue;\n            int cost = rec(i + 1, p - a, n - b, nc + 50) + (a + b) * (i + 1);\n            if (cost < best) best = cost;\n        }\n    }\n    mem[i][p][n][c] = best;\n    return best;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long val;\n    cin >> val;\n    int cap = 50;\n    memset(mem, -1, sizeof(mem));\n    s = to_string(val);\n    while (s.length() < 17) s = \"0\" + s;\n    reverse(s.b